      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Sixty-eight hemosorptions were carried out in 55 patients with atherosclerotic lesions of the lower extremity vessels. Hemosorption efficacy was evaluated by biochemical methods, clinical manifestations of ischemia of the legs, heart and brain. It was established that hemosorption proved highly efficient in the complex treatment of obliterative lesions of the lower extremity vessels, particularly, in the II-III stages of the disease."},
